schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Retroactive (public goods) funding
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A funding model where contributors get paid for work they already did,
    even if funding wasn't arranged upfront, rather than the traditional
    grant-application-before-work pattern.
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Listed in coordination-transparency.md under "New Economic Models /
    Credentialing" alongside POAPs and Gitcoin's peer-reviewed public-goods
    funding as an example of value capture becoming possible for people/
    communities who previously could not access it upfront.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - grant-funding (the traditional, apply-before-you-build model this contrasts with)
    - poap (proof-of-attendance token, a related but distinct credentialing primitive named in the same section)
  important_distinctions:
    - "retroactive funding rewards proven-useful past work; traditional grants fund proposed future work"
  tensions:
    - rewards-what-already-proved-useful vs risk-of-underfunding-untested-new-ideas
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    The article names the concept without specifying who judges "usefulness"
    retroactively or what mechanism (e.g. Optimism's RetroPGF rounds) actually
    implements it — worth expanding with a concrete implementation record later.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/coordination-transparency.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-97dd78ba716a
  source_lineage: coordination-transparency.md
